HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;
```

### Q6. Find duplicate rows based on salary using ROW_NUMBER.

```sql
WITH duplicate_rows AS (
SELECT employee_id,
ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY salary ORDER BY employee_id) AS row_num
FROM employees
)
SELECT * FROM duplicate_rows WHERE row_num > 1;
```

### Q7. Find employees who have the same salary as another employee.

